# Run a request with the green arrow next to it (Rider, Visual Studio)
# or "Send Request" (VS Code with the REST Client extension).

@api = http://localhost:8000/api
@token = paste-the-access_token-from-login-here

### Log in as the seeded member (use admin@test.com for the admin routes)
POST {{api}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "member@test.com", "password": "password123" }

### Who am I?
GET {{api}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Dashboard numbers
GET {{api}}/me/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Log a workout
POST {{api}}/me/workouts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Push Day",
  "duration_minutes": 50,
  "exercises": [
    { "exercise_id": 1, "sets": [ { "weight": 185, "reps": 8 }, { "weight": 185, "reps": 7 } ] }
  ]
}

### Validation error: Laravel-style 422
POST {{api}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "email": "not-an-email", "password": "123" }

### Public catalog, no token needed
GET {{api}}/exercises?search=press&difficulty=beginner&perPage=4